<title>UK: UK PSBR 2.119 bln stg in December.</title>
<headline>UK PSBR 2.119 bln stg in December.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK public sector borrowing requirement data for December. Deficits unless noted.</p>
<p> PSBR (in million stg)	    DEC     APR-DEC    APR-DEC</p>
<p>						    1996/97    1995/96</p>
<p> Public sector			2,119    16,136    23,028</p>
<p> Central government		 1,787    17,773    25,757</p>
<p> Central government own acct    1,786    17,857    24,338</p>
<p> Local Authority			303	 310	 574</p>
<p>  from central govt		    34rep  1,283     1,084</p>
<p> General Government		 2,124    16,800    25,247</p>
<p> Public Corporation		    30     2,031rep  1,884rep</p>
<p>  from central govt		    35     1,364rep    335</p>
<p>GOVERNMENT RECEIPTS</p>
<p> Central govt total receipts   23,838   193,025    181,105</p>
<p> Inland Revenue receipts	  8,693    72,848     68,585</p>
<p>  of which income tax	     6,120    48,749     49,046</p>
<p>  corporation tax		   1,249    19,066     15,757</p>
<p> Customs and excise		 8,907    64,227     59,604</p>
<p>  of which VAT			3,266    35,677     32,398</p>
<p> Social security		    3,377    32,760     31,315</p>
<p> Interest				 525     5,514	5,481</p>
<p> Other				  2,336    17,676     16,120</p>
<p>CENTRAL GOVERNMENT OUTLAYS</p>
<p>  Total				25,624   210,882    205,442</p>
<p>   of which Interest		3,092    20,064     16,975</p>
<p>   Net departmental outlays    22,792   195,048    189,071</p>
<p>NOTE- Privatisation proceeds in December were 260 million stg, compared with 556 million in December last year.</p>
<p>Consensus forecast was for a 1.1 bln stg PSBR in December.</p>
<p>November's PSBR was revised to 2.709 billion stg from the originally reported 2.6 billion stg.</p>
<p>The ONS said privatisation proceeds were mainly due to the sale of residual shareholdings.</p>
<p>The ONS said interest payments of 3.092 billion stg in December had a significant upward effect on government outlays and therefore the PSBR. Last December, 1.930 billion in interest was paid.</p>
<p>That was largely due to interest payments on strippable gilts.</p>
